  "authoringDirection": "Whole surviving Pyramid of the Moon, its receding worn masonry tiers, summit, central upper stair flights and intrinsic projecting stepped talud-tablero front platform with axial stair. Preserve complete native outline including projections and irregular rear notch. Exclude separate plaza pyramids/altars, Pyramid of the Sun, Palace of Quetzalpap\u00e1lotl, avenue, mountains, trees, visitors, temporary access barriers and interiors. Warm grey-brown rough volcanic rubble, subdued pale stone ledges and recessed dark tablero panels. Four stepped projecting talud-tablero bodies, real central tread/riser stairs, upper two axial flights/landings, broad battered main tiers and worn open summit. Do not substitute a regular four-sided ideal pyramid, add a summit temple, fill the entire plaza or use the posterized green image for colors.",
